  "reason": "Evidence: scVI n200 (0.520) outperforms PCA n2000 (0.485) as RNA encoder, and RNA modality dominates image (0.520 vs 0.208). The biggest untested design axis is whether multiprofile aggregation adds value over single profile. Question: Does multiprofile with simple avgpool aggregation improve upon the best single-profile scVI result (config_004, acc 0.520)? This directly extends our strongest configuration by changing only the profile setting (single→multi) and adding the simplest aggregation (avgpool), isolating the multiprofile effect. Rationale: With 6 experiments remaining, establishing whether multiprofile helps at all is critical—it gates whether we invest further budget in transformer aggregation, scGPT multiprofile, or multimodal multiprofile variants. If avgpool doesn't help, transformer is unlikely to either, saving budget for encoder exploration or multimodal fusion tests."
